ue,"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":true,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"issue_tracking":{"public_tracker":true,"resolve_time":null}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/imagem","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":null,"@type":"metrics","distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":false,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[],"readme":true,"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":true,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"issue_tracking":{"public_tracker":true,"resolve_time":null}}}]},"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p><span><span><span>The ImageM application proposes an integrated user interface that facilitates the processing and the analysis of multi-dimensional images within the Matlab environment. It provides a user-friendly visualization of multi-dimensional images, a collection of image processing algorithms and methods for analysis of images, the management of spatial calibration, and facilities for the analysis of multi-variate images. Its graphical user interface is </span></span></span>largely inspired from the open source software \"ImageJ\".&nbsp;<span><span><span>ImageM can also be run on the open source alternative software to Matlab, Octave.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span><span><span>ImageM is freely distributed on GitHub: <a href=\"https://github.com/mattools/ImageM\">https://github.com/mattools/ImageM</a>.</span></span></span></p>","summary":"","value":"<p><span><span><span>The ImageM application proposes an integrated user interface that facilitates the processing and the analysis of multi-dimensional images within the Matlab environment. It provides a user-friendly visualization of multi-dimensional images, a collection of image processing algorithms and methods for analysis of images, the management of spatial calibration, and facilities for the analysis of multi-variate images. Its graphical user interface is </span></span></span>largely inspired from the open source software \"ImageJ\".&nbsp;<span><span><span>ImageM can also be run on the open source alternative software to Matlab, Octave.</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span><span><span>ImageM is freely distributed on GitHub: <a href=\"https://github.com/mattools/ImageM\">https://github.com/mattools/ImageM</a>.</span></span></span></p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2024-10-31T12:32:50+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2020-03-05T09:56:02+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[{"cid":null,"comment_count":null,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":null,"last_comment_uid":null,"status":2}],"free_tagging":[{"target_id":3599,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"9452479a-42da-42cf-a214-898c8df8025c","url":"/taxonomy/term/3599"},{"target_id":5157,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"a8a76882-0de8-4205-919f-5c4d9984afd3","url":"/taxonomy/term/5157"}],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1583402553,"last_comment_uid":19,"status":2}],"has_author":[{"value":"David Legland"}],"has_biological_terms":[],"has_comparison":[],"has_documentation":[{"options":[],"title":"","uri":"https://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/fileexchange/45847-imagem"}],"has_doi":[],"has_entry_curator":[],"has_function":[{"target_id":4111,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3443","url":"/image-analysis"},{"target_id":4004,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"http://edamontology.org/operation_Image_s